#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:16
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:18
msgid ""
"This PEP describes the detailed plan for migrating from Python's issue "
"tracker on Roundup to GitHub issues.  See :pep:`581` for rationale and "
"background.  :pep:`588` also describes the detailed timeline for the "
"migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:25
msgid "Migration Plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:27
msgid ""
"Here we outline the tasks, steps, and core decisions we need to make in "
"order to migrate bug tracking to GitHub, with the least impact on CPython "
"developer productivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:32
msgid "Hire a professional project manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:34
msgid ""
"Having a professional project manager to handle the migration, similar to "
"how the Warehouse project was managed, would help ensure the success of this "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:38
msgid "Create a playground CPython issue tracker on GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:40
msgid ""
"We should create a playground issue tracker on GitHub where we can "
"experiment and test out the new workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:44
msgid "Backup of GitHub data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:46
msgid ""
"This effort has been started and is being tracked as an issue in core-"
"workflow [#]_. We're using GitHub's Migrations API [#]_ to download GitHub "
"data for CPython on a daily basis. The archives will be dropped in a S3 "
"bucket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:51
msgid "Thanks to Ee Durbin for working on this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:55
msgid "Update the CLA host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:57
msgid ""
"At the moment, the CLA is hosted within bpo. It needs to be updated such "
"that signing the CLA does not require a bpo account, and it should be hosted "
"outside of the bpo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:61
msgid ""
"The current CLA process itself is not ideal. Currently, contributors to "
"devguide, peps, and core-workflow need to sign a CLA, and it requires a bpo "
"account. A bpo account should not be required for those projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:65
msgid ""
"There is an ongoing effort to start using our own instance of CLA assistant "
"instead of the current CLA process in place. Discussion about this has been "
"started in `core-workflow mailing list <https://mail.python.org/archives/"
"list/core-workflow@python.org/thread/JBV3XJVD2DLDX5DY7TZEA6CO5YPNHJ2C/>`_ as "
"well as on `Discourse <https://discuss.python.org/t/using-cla-assistant-for-"
"python/990>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:72
msgid ""
"This effort `is currently stalled <https://discuss.python.org/t/cla-"
"assistant-is-no-go/2066/>`_ because cla-assistant does not yet support CLA "
"signed on behalf of organization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:77
msgid "Create \"Python Triage\" team on GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:79
msgid ""
"The bug triagers on bpo are valuable to the core Python workflow, and we "
"definitely would need even more help with triaging issues on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:82
msgid ""
"It has been `proposed on Discourse <https://discuss.python.org/t/proposal-"
"create-bug-triage-team-on-github/992/5>`_ for us to create a \"bug triage\" "
"team on GitHub to help with closing issues, notifying the appropriate "
"parties, as well as applying labels to issues and pull requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:88
msgid ""
"The new Triage role on GitHub is currently in beta, and the Python "
"organization has been granted access to this role, and we can begin taking "
"advantage of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:91
msgid ""
"The \"Python Triage\" team has been created. A description and expectations "
"of the triage role `have been added to Devguide <https://devguide.python.org/"
"triaging/#python-triage-team>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:94
msgid ""
"Progress of this project can be tracked in `\"Adding Triagers\" project "
"board <https://github.com/python/core-workflow/projects/3>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:99
msgid "Create labels for issue triage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:101
msgid "In bpo, we currently have the following fields for each issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:103
msgid ""
"Types: ``behavior``, ``crash``, ``compile error``, ``resource usage``, "
"``security``, ``performance``, ``enhancement``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:106
msgid ""
"Components: ``2to3``, ``Argument Clinic``, ``asyncio``, ``Build``, ``Cross-"
"build``, ``ctypes``, ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:109
msgid ""
"Priority: ``release blocker``, ``deferred blocker``, ``critical``, ``high``, "
"``normal``, ``low``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:112
msgid "We will create the corresponding labels::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:120
msgid "In addition, we'll create a ``needs triage`` label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:122
msgid ""
"The final \"labels\" to be created can be decided at a later time when it is "
"time to start switching to GitHub issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:125
msgid ""
"A test repository containing all possible labels and color schema has been "
"created by Carol Willing and can be reviewed at https://github.com/willingc/"
"test-581/labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:129
msgid "Create issue templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:131
msgid "We will create an issue template and add the following headers::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:140
msgid ""
"The idea is to allow the issue creator to help us triage the issue. The "
"above values are pre-filled in the template. The issue creator will remove "
"texts that do not apply to their issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:144
msgid ""
"Based on the above headers, bedevere-bot can apply the necessary labels to "
"the issue. If the issue creator did not supply the above headers, the bot "
"will apply the ``needs triage`` label. At that point, it will require a core "
"developer to properly label the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:149
msgid ""
"We can also take advantage of GitHub's multiple issue template feature, and "
"the ability to automatically set issue assignee and labels by using issue "
"templates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:155
msgid "Updates to bedevere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:157
msgid ""
"Bedevere-bot will need to be updated to recognize the issue headers "
"described above and apply the proper labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:160
msgid ""
"Bedevere-bot can also copy over the labels to pull requests that correspond "
"to the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:165
msgid "Update the devguide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:167
msgid ""
"Devguide should be updated with information about the new workflow of using "
"GitHub issues. It can be done as a separate branch, and it should be done "
"ahead of the migration, not after."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:172
msgid "Add a button in bpo to migrate the issue to GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:174
msgid ""
"This will require the bpo to be updated. But I believe the effort needed for "
"this is much less than a complete overhaul."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:177
msgid ""
"We will create a button in bpo, that will copy over the issue description "
"and associated comments into a GitHub issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:180
msgid ""
"We need to add a new status: \"moved\" with the url of the GitHub issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:182
msgid ""
"We should not be moving all open issues to GitHub. Only when someone is "
"interested in continuing work or discussion about the issue, that the issue "
"should be \"moved\" to GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:188
msgid "Migrated issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:190
msgid ""
"When an issue is marked as \"moved\", this issue should be in read-only "
"mode. bpo should forbid the edition of the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:195
msgid "Make bpo read-only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:197
msgid ""
"This should be the final step. Once we start using GitHub issues, make bpo "
"read-only, instead of shutting it down. Do not accept new registrations. Do "
"not allow comments or issues to be created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:203
msgid "Mapping between issues from bpo and GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:205
msgid ""
"Usually when we reference an issue from bpo, we use bpo-XYZ but with GitHub, "
"we will have a new reference with this format ``https://github.com/python/"
"cpython/issue/XYZ``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:209
msgid ""
"Because we will migrate the issues from bpo to GitHub, we need to have a new "
"field on bpo for the reference to the issues on GitHub, and the same thing "
"on GitHub for the 'eventual' reference from bpo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:213
msgid ""
"For GitHub, we need to add ``origin: https://bugs.python.org/issueXYZ``. For "
"bpo, add a new field ``moved to: https://github.com/python/cpython/issue/"
"XYZ``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:218
msgid "Nosy-ing the expert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:220
msgid ""
"A current functionality in bpo is to automatically nosy people who are "
"listed as an expert of certain area. Several Python core developers have "
"expressed that they prefer not having to subscribe to everything on GitHub, "
"but only getting notified for issues related to their area of interest and "
"expertise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:225
msgid ""
"To help with this situation, we can develop a bot that can notify people "
"whenever an issue has been categorized using labels. For example, when an "
"issue was labeled with ``area-windows``, the windows experts can be "
"notified. The notification can be in the form of email notification, or @-"
"mention on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:231
msgid "Open issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:234
msgid "A GitHub account should not be a requirement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:236
msgid ""
"Back when moving the CPython codebase from Mercurial to GitHub was being "
"discussed [#]_ [#]_, it was brought up that we still needed to allow "
"uploading of patches on bpo, and that a GitHub account should not be a "
"requirement in order to contribute to Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:241
msgid ""
"If bpo is made read-only, we'll need to come up with a different solution to "
"allow people to contribute when they don't have a GitHub account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:244
msgid ""
"One solution is to create a new \"python-issues\" mailing list, similar to "
"the docs@python.org [#]_ mailing list, to allow people to submit their "
"issues there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:248
msgid ""
"Related to this, since the migration to GitHub in 2017, I recall one case "
"[#]_ where there was a contributor, who submitted a patch to Mercurial and "
"refused to create a GitHub account. Because of this, our bot was unable to "
"detect whether they had signed the CLA. Another person had volunteered to "
"upload their patch to GitHub. But it was still required that both people "
"sign the CLA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:255
msgid ""
"That particular situation was complicated. It took up five core developers' "
"time to investigate and manually check the CLA, causing confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:261
msgid "Trim off the \"Components\" list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:263
msgid ""
"Is the current \"components\" list still making sense and relevant? Can the "
"list be shortened?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:268
msgid "Priority list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:270
msgid ""
"Is the current \"priority\" list useful? Alyssa Coghlan noted that perhaps "
"only ``release blocker`` and ``deferred blocker`` are useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:275
msgid "Further questions and discussions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0588.rst:277
msgid ""
"You can post questions on Discourse under the `Core-Workflow <https://"
"discuss.python.org/c/core-workflow>`_ category."
msgstr ""

